.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

int bc_pty_close(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Closes the active PTY session on the server.
The server terminates the child process (if still running), closes the
PTY master file descriptor, and releases all associated resources.
.PP
If the child process is still running when \f[CR]bc_pty_close\f[R] is
called, the server sends \f[CR]SIGHUP\f[R] followed by
\f[CR]SIGKILL\f[R] (after a brief grace period) to ensure clean
termination.
The \f[CR]bc_pty_on_exit(3)\f[R] callback, if registered, fires with the
child\(cqs exit status before the close acknowledgement is sent.
.PP
After this call returns successfully, the client may spawn a new PTY
session with \f[CR]bc_pty_spawn(3)\f[R].
.PP
If no PTY session is active, this function returns
\f[CR]BC_ERR_PROTOCOL\f[R].
.SH Wire protocol
Sends on \f[CR]CHAN_PTY\f[R] (channel 5):
.IP
.EX
{\(dqaction\(dq:\(dqclose\(dq}
.EE
.PP
Receives acknowledgement:
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqclosed\(dq}
.EE
.PP
If the child was still running, an exit event may precede the close
acknowledgement:
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqexit\(dq,\(dqexit_code\(dq:137}
{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqclosed\(dq}
.EE
