.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The close is idempotent at the transport level: if the connection drops
during close, the server still cleans up when the socket closes.
.IP \(bu 2
After \f[CR]bc_pty_close\f[R] returns, any registered output and exit
callbacks remain registered but will not fire until a new PTY session is
spawned.
Call \f[CR]bc_pty_on_output(c, NULL, NULL)\f[R] and
\f[CR]bc_pty_on_exit(c, NULL, NULL)\f[R] to explicitly unregister them.
.IP \(bu 2
The exit event delivered before the close acknowledgement reports the
child\(cqs actual exit status.
If killed by signal, the exit code is 128 + signal number (e.g., 137 for
\f[CR]SIGKILL\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
This function blocks until the server acknowledgement is received or the
timeout expires.
For non\-blocking close semantics, use \f[CR]bc_send_msg(3)\f[R]
directly and handle the response in \f[CR]bc_poll(3)\f[R].
